{"id":"CQ-001","category":"code_quality","criterion":"correctness","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/evals/graders/recall-vs-defects.sh","line":74,"code_snippet":"r'|(?:(?<![A-Za-z0-9_./:])(?:head|base)|(?<![A-Za-z0-9_./:])):(?P<bare>' + RNG + r')(?![A-Za-z0-9])')","reasoning_trace":"Read the 1.1.0 CITE regex; the bare-:N alternative's negative lookbehind omits quote, asterisk, paren and brace, so every `\"key\":N` pair in the LOA-VERDICT trailer and tokens like `**Severity**:2` bind to the last cited path at lines 0-2. Reproduced with a two-defect manifest: head grader recall 1.0 / 6 citations, base grader 0.5 / 1 citation; on a clean fixture without a trailer false_positives 2 vs 1. RG-1..15 pass on head because no fixture anchor lies within lines 0-5 of the last cited file.","finding":"Phantom citations from trailer JSON and markdown tokens inflate recall (and FP counts without a trailer) in the grader that decided the Task 4.8 replay A/B revert.","critique":"The regression tests never place the mandated trailer after a citation with an early anchor.","remediation":"Strip the `<!-- LOA-VERDICT ... -->` comment from `text` before `CITE.finditer`, or extend the lookbehind to `(?<![A-Za-z0-9_./:\"'*){,\\]])`; add RG test: `a.sh:400` + trailer must yield citations == 1 and must not detect an anchor at line <= 5; re-run the replay A/B.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1286.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-001","category":"security","criterion":"authorization","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/hooks/compliance/implement-gate.sh","line":115,"code_snippet":"configured_mode=$(yq '.implement_gate.mode // \"\"' \"$PROJECT_ROOT/.loa.config.yaml\" 2>/dev/null) || configured_mode=\"\"","reasoning_trace":"Traced S1 (model-authored tool_input.active_skill) to K2 (silent exit 0 at :129) under authoritative mode. The mode is selected by a key in .loa.config.yaml; in the head tree an Edit of that file is a non-App-Zone write the same hook allows silently (:108). Reproduced: Edit payload for .loa.config.yaml -> exit 0 silent; then Write src/index.ts with active_skill=implement -> exit 0 silent; the same write without the key -> decision ask. IG-11 pins the key as undocumented. Cross-model DISS-C-001 (claude-headless) reached the same path.","finding":"An undocumented opt-in turns a model-authored field into an authorization signal, and the file holding the opt-in is unfenced by this hook, so the fenced agent can enable the mode and self-attest.","critique":"The PR's own header states the field is model-authored and evidence-only; keeping an authoritative branch contradicts that.","remediation":"Remove the authoritative branch until a harness-set field exists; or require RUNNING state AND the attestation, treat .loa.config.yaml as a trust input (ask), log each authoritative allow to audit.jsonl, and document the key with its warning in .loa.config.yaml.example (drop IG-11).","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/807.html","https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control/"]}
{"id":"ARCH-001","category":"architecture","criterion":"standards_compliance","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/defaults/model-config.yaml","line":470,"code_snippet":"# \"Claude 4.6 and later models ... include the full 1M token context window at standard pricing\", so no long_context tier","reasoning_trace":"Compared the new claude-opus-5-5 entry (no pricing.long_context, vendor statement about 4.6+) with claude-opus-5 (:562), claude-sonnet-5, claude-fable-5, claude-fable-5-1, which keep long_context 2.0x/1.5x verified:false from the same vendor source. test_anthropic_catalog_floor.py:326 pins the tier on FIVE_FAMILY and :348 pins its absence on 5.5 (FIVE_FAMILY excludes 5.5, so both tests pass and the contradiction is locked in). Confirmed by cross-model review DISS-C-002 in the review phase.","finding":"Two incompatible long-context pricing models for one vendor family and one cited source; metering diverges between opus and its first fallback hop above 200K input.","critique":"The decision should be made once for the 4.6+ family.","remediation":"Either drop long_context from the FIVE_FAMILY entries (update test :326) or add it to 5.5 with verified:false and record in catalog-evidence.md why the vendor statement is not trusted.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1068.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-002","category":"code_quality","criterion":"error_handling","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/check-permissions.sh","line":235,"code_snippet":"rule_key \"$perm\"","reasoning_trace":"rule_key returns 1 for anything not shaped Bash(...) (:164); main runs under set -euo pipefail (:15); the call is a bare statement. All 16 REQUIRED_* entries are Bash(...:*) today, so the path is dead.","finding":"The first non-Bash requirement added aborts the preflight with exit 1 and no report (or reuses the previous RULE_KEY if set -e is relaxed).","remediation":"rule_key \"$perm\" || { missing_permissions+=(\"$perm\"); continue; }; reset RULE_KEY=\"\" at the top of rule_key.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/252.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-003","category":"code_quality","criterion":"correctness","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/check-permissions.sh","line":237,"code_snippet":"base=\"*${key#\\*}\"; base=\"${base%% *}\"","reasoning_trace":"For an exact requirement key `=git push`, `${key#\\*}` is a no-op and base becomes `*=git`, a key no rule normalises to; a wildcard deny Bash(git:*) would then not deny an exact requirement. No exact requirement exists today. Cross-model DISS-C-002.","finding":"Base-wildcard derivation is wrong for exact-form requirements (dead path).","remediation":"body=\"${key#[*=]}\"; base=\"*${body%% *}\"; add a bats case with an exact requirement and a wildcard deny.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/697.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-002","category":"security","criterion":"authorization","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/data/model-permissions.yaml","line":446,"code_snippet":"anthropic:claude-headless:\n    execution_mode: remote_model\n    capabilities: { file_read: false, file_write: false, command_execution: false, network_access: false }","reasoning_trace":"The row's own notes (:467-469) say the adapter runs `claude -p --tools \"\" --permission-mode plan` and that extra.allowed_tools widens the CLI. Nothing validates the row against the catalog's extra.allowed_tools. Rows have no runtime effect unless hounfour.feature_flags.context_filtering is on. Cross-model DISS-C-003.","finding":"A local CLI hop is registered as a no-side-effect remote model with no check tying the claim to the catalog knob that can falsify it.","remediation":"Add a parity test or adapter refusal: when the catalog's claude-headless extra.allowed_tools is non-empty, the registry row must declare the widened capabilities (or a separate row must exist).","confidence":"medium","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1059.html"]}
{"id":"DEVOPS-001","category":"devops","criterion":"maintainability","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/tools/check-prompt-budget.sh","line":53,"code_snippet":"SKILL_LIMIT, LOA_LIMIT, PROTO_FAIL, PROTO_WARN = 16384, 10240, 160000, 114688","reasoning_trace":"wc -c pr/head/.claude/loa/CLAUDE.loa.md = 10225 B against the raised 10240 B limit.","finding":"15 bytes of headroom; the next rationale regeneration that lengthens a `why` string fails PB-4.","remediation":"Set the limit from the measured size plus a stated margin, or trim non-rendered whitespace.","confidence":"high","references":[]}
{"id":"ARCH-002","category":"architecture","criterion":"standards_compliance","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/data/agent-types.yaml","line":26,"code_snippet":"  prompt-auditor-io:\n    write_capable: false","reasoning_trace":"The registry lists eight types; skill-capabilities.bats:854 iterates every .claude/agents/*.md and fails on an unlisted one, and :850 pins the exact eight-entry string. The install this audit runs on carries .claude/agents/chart-researcher.md and a later revision of the YAML that lists it. Whether the PR's own tree had that agent is not knowable from the touched-file snapshot; the pinned string suggests it did not.","finding":"SC-T-AGENT-7 is red on any checkout that carries a project agent the YAML omits (chart-researcher today).","remediation":"Add chart-researcher: {write_capable: false} (and any other .claude/agents/*.md present at merge).","confidence":"low","references":[]}
{"id":"SUMMARY","category":"security","criterion":"overall","severity":"INFO","score":3,"finding":"sprint-1 audit: 0 critical, 1 high, 2 medium, 5 low; verdict CHANGES_REQUIRED; dissent 2 voices consensus, 0 rejected, not degraded","reasoning_trace":"Rubric scores: SEC-IV 4, SEC-AZ 3, SEC-CI 5, SEC-IN 5, SEC-AV 4, ARCH-ST 3, CQ-RD 4, CQ-TQ 3, DEVOPS 4.","confidence":"high"}

